From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:45:05 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] internal/syscall/windows: move a held file aside before deleting it

Where Windows refuses the newer delete (0011), RemoveAll and Root.Remove
delete through a fallback (CL 713480, commit b31dc77, Go 1.26) that only
marks a file. The file keeps its name while any program still has it open,
so RemoveAll cannot remove the directory it was in.

Free the name at once even while another program has the file open. Move
such a file out of the way first, into the temporary folder if it is on the
same drive and within its own folder if not, then delete it.

	                       before                 after
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 7, 8, 8.1,     the name stays, so     the name is free at once
	some early Windows 10  RemoveAll fails
	(file open elsewhere)
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 10 22H2, 11    the name is free at    the name is free at once
	                       once

Gate: version, then query (10 before 22H2, 0011's check) | Remembered: Y

